      "extract": "Although the nice-slice argument seems very general, we will present evidence from string theory that it fails. A key assumption that goes into the nice-slice argument is that the underlying microscopic theory is approximately a local ﬁeld theory. Speciﬁcally, it assumes that any nonlocality which results from the non-zero size of strings is limited to small space-like separations, but this is incorrect, as we shall",
      "extractCut": true
    },
