          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "Having obtained the commutators of nice-slice ﬁelds from string ﬁeld theory, we are now in a position to understand their signiﬁcance for the nice-slice argument. In this section we will argue that the assumption of locality of the low-energy nice-slice theory is not valid in string theory. Evidence for this will be obtained in two ways. First, we compare the commutators of nice slice ﬁelds derived from string ﬁeld",
